@lang en
IMPORT `bm-ear-general-exclusions`

-- Bao Minh erection all risks rules: the period of insurance (src:40-57), page 1-2.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are generated by tools/vnsrc.py from line N of
-- ../../source/raw/baominh-ear.txt.
--
-- WHAT THIS PART DOES. Cover on an item begins when the works commence or the item is
-- unloaded at the site, whatever date the schedule gives. It ends at the first of: the
-- handover of the works; the completion of the first test operation or test loading;
-- four weeks (or another period agreed in writing) after testing began; and, at the latest,
-- the date in the schedule (as extended with Bao Minh's prior written consent). A part that
-- has been tested, operated or handed over goes off cover, and so does every liability
-- arising from it. A second-hand item goes off cover as soon as its testing begins.
--
-- DAYS AND INSTANTS. Every fact here is a calendar DATE. The document times some limits by
-- an EVENT (commencement, unloading, handover, a test) and some by a DATE or a period of
-- DAYS (the schedule date; four weeks). Where the occurrence fell on the same day as an
-- event that starts or ends cover, a date cannot say which came first, and the rules
-- refuse by name rather than guess (fork F07). A date limit is read as including its last
-- day (fork F09). "4 weeks" is 28 calendar days (fork F08).

§ `The period of insurance`
-- src:40 | THỜI HẠN BẢO HIỂM

§§ `Finding an item in the schedule`

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
      `the schedule` IS A `The schedule`
GIVETH A MAYBE `An item in Part I of the schedule`
`the item numbered` `the number` `in` `the schedule` MEANS
    listToMaybe (filter (GIVEN i YIELD i's `number` EQUALS `the number`) (`the schedule`'s `the items in Part I`))

§§ `When cover begins`

-- "Bảo Minh's liability begins from the commencement of the works OR after the items named
-- in the schedule have been unloaded at the site, even though the date in the schedule may
-- differ." Read as: for an item, the EARLIER of the two events that has happened (fork F06).
-- src:42 | Trách nhiệm của Bảo Minh sẽ bắt đầu từ lúc khởi công công trình hoặc sau khi dỡ xong các hạng
-- src:43 | mục có tên trong Phụ lục xuống công trường, dù ngày quy định trong phụ lục có thể khác và sẽ tiếp
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance, first sentence (src:42-43)
GIVEN `the works` IS A `The works`
      `the item`  IS AN `An item in Part I of the schedule`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day cover on the item began` MEANS
    `the earliest of` (LIST `the works`'s `date the works commenced`,
                            `the item`'s `date unloaded at the site`)

-- For Part II, the period of the policy as a whole: from the earlier of the commencement of
-- the works and the first unloading of any item named in the schedule.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance, first sentence (src:42-43)
GIVEN `the policy` IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day cover under the policy began` MEANS
    `the earliest of` (`the works`'s `date the works commenced`
                       FOLLOWED BY map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `date unloaded at the site`)
                                       (`the policy`'s `the schedule`'s `the items in Part I`))
    WHERE `the works` MEANS `the policy`'s `the works`

GIVEN `the dates` IS A LIST OF MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest of` `the dates` MEANS
    CONSIDER catMaybes `the dates`
    WHEN EMPTY                THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY others THEN JUST (foldr `the earlier of` d others)

§§ `When cover ends for the works as a whole`

-- "... and continues until after the handover of the works or after the completion of the
-- first operation or test loading, whichever occurs first, but not later than 4 weeks
-- (unless otherwise agreed in writing) from the day testing began."
-- src:44 | tục có hiệu lực cho tới sau khi bàn giao công trình hoặc sau khi hoàn tất lần vận hành hay chạy thử
-- src:45 | có tải đầu tiên tùy theo thời điểm nào xảy ra trước, nhưng sẽ không chậm quá 4 tuần (trừ khi có
-- src:46 | thỏa thuận khác bằng văn bản) kể từ ngày bắt đầu chạy thử. Tuy nhiên, nếu một bộ phận của xưởng
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance (src:43-46)
GIVEN `the policy` IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the events that end cover on the works` MEANS
    catMaybes (LIST `the works`'s `date the works were handed over`,
                    `the works`'s `date the first test operation or test loading was completed`)
    WHERE `the works` MEANS `the policy`'s `the works`

-- The testing limit counts calendar days from the day testing began; 4 weeks is 28 days.
-- An occurrence on the 28th day after that day is inside the limit (fork F09).
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance, "không chậm quá 4 tuần" (src:45-46)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`four weeks, in days` MEANS 28

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance (src:45-46)
GIVEN `the policy` IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the testing period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the policy`'s `the works`'s `date testing began`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (t PLUS `the testing period, in days`)
    WHERE
        `the testing period, in days` MEANS
            fromMaybe `four weeks, in days` (`the policy`'s `a testing period agreed in writing in place of four weeks, in days`)

-- "At the latest, this insurance ends on the date stated in the schedule. Every extension
-- of the period must be agreed by Bao Minh in advance and in writing." The stated date is
-- read as the last day of cover (fork F09). An extension agreed in advance in writing
-- replaces the stated date; the record holds no other kind of extension.
-- src:56 | Chậm nhất thì bảo hiểm này sẽ chấm dứt hiệu lực vào ngày quy định ghi trong Phụ lục. Mọi sự kéo
-- src:57 | dài thời hạn (gia hạn) bảo hiểm đều phải được Bảo Minh đồng ý trước bằng văn bản.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance, last paragraph (src:56-57)
GIVEN `the policy` IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of cover under the schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the policy`'s `an extension agreed in advance in writing by Bao Minh, to`
    WHEN JUST e  THEN e
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the policy`'s `the schedule`'s `the date on which cover ends`

GIVEN `the policy` IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the last days of cover on the works` MEANS
    `the last day of cover under the schedule` `the policy`
    FOLLOWED BY catMaybes (LIST `the last day of the testing period` `the policy`)

§§ `When cover ends for a part`

-- "However, if a part of the plant or some machines have been tested and/or operated or
-- handed over, cover on that part, or on those items of equipment or machinery, and every
-- liability arising from them, ends, although this insurance remains liable for the
-- remaining parts." "Tested" is read as: its test run has been COMPLETED (fork F10).
-- src:47 | máy hay một số cỗ máy đã được chạy thử và/hoặc vận hành hay bàn giao thì việc bảo hiểm cho
-- src:50 | phần đó hay các thiết bị hoặc máy móc và mọi trách nhiệm phát sinh từ đó sẽ chấm dứt hiệu lực,
-- src:51 | mặc dù bảo hiểm này vẫn chịu trách nhiệm đối với các bộ phận còn lại.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance, partial termination (src:46-51)
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item in Part I of the schedule`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the events that end cover on the item as a part` MEANS
    catMaybes (LIST `the item`'s `date its test run was completed`,
                    `the item`'s `date it was first operated`,
                    `the item`'s `date it was handed over`)

-- "For second-hand items, cover ends as soon as those items begin testing."
-- src:53 | Đối với các hạng mục sử dụng lại (second-hand items) thì hiệu lực bảo hiểm chấm dứt ngay sau khi
-- src:54 | các hạng mục đó bắt đầu chạy thử.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance, second-hand items (src:53-54)
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item in Part I of the schedule`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the events that end cover on a second-hand item` MEANS
    IF   `the item`'s `second-hand`
    THEN catMaybes (LIST `the item`'s `date its testing began`)
    ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN `the policy` IS A `The policy`
      `the item`   IS AN `An item in Part I of the schedule`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the events that end cover on the item` MEANS
    append (`the events that end cover on the works` `the policy`)
           (append (`the events that end cover on the item as a part` `the item`)
                   (`the events that end cover on a second-hand item` `the item`))

§§ `Whether a day falls within the period`

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance: a start or end EVENT on the day of the occurrence (fork F07)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the occurrence fell on the day cover began, and the record does not say whether it came before or after` MEANS
    REFUSE "the occurrence fell on the day cover began, and the record does not say whether it came before or after"

@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance: a start or end EVENT on the day of the occurrence (fork F07)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the occurrence fell on the day of an event that ends cover, and the record does not say which came first` MEANS
    REFUSE "the occurrence fell on the day of an event that ends cover, and the record does not say which came first"

-- The general test: does `the day` fall within a period that begins with `the start`, ends
-- on (and includes) each of `the last days`, and ends AT each of `the end events`? Definite
-- answers first; a same-day refusal only where nothing else already places the day outside.
GIVEN `the day`        IS A DATE
      `the start`      IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last days`  IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the end events` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls within the period` `the day` `the start` `the last days` `the end events` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the start`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s  THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the day` LESS THAN s                                     THEN FALSE
            IF any (GIVEN e YIELD `the day` GREATER THAN e) `the last days`  THEN FALSE
            IF any (GIVEN e YIELD `the day` GREATER THAN e) `the end events` THEN FALSE
            IF `the day` EQUALS s
                THEN `the occurrence fell on the day cover began, and the record does not say whether it came before or after`
            IF any (GIVEN e YIELD `the day` EQUALS e) `the end events`
                THEN `the occurrence fell on the day of an event that ends cover, and the record does not say which came first`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Part I: was the item on cover on the day of the occurrence?
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance (src:42-57); Part I insuring clause "at any time during the period of insurance" (src:155-156)
GIVEN `the day`    IS A DATE
      `the policy` IS A `The policy`
      `the item`   IS AN `An item in Part I of the schedule`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the item was on cover on` `the day` `under` `the policy` `for` `the item` MEANS
    `falls within the period` `the day`
        (`the day cover on the item began` (`the policy`'s `the works`) `the item`)
        (`the last days of cover on the works` `the policy`)
        (`the events that end cover on the item` `the policy` `the item`)

-- Part II: was the policy on cover on the day of the occurrence, for a liability arising
-- (if it arises from a particular item) from that item? An item number that is not in the
-- schedule contributes no end of its own.
@ref Bao Minh EAR rules, period of insurance (src:42-57), with "every liability arising from them" (src:50); Part II "during the period of insurance" (src:256)
GIVEN `the day`      IS A DATE
      `the policy`   IS A `The policy`
      `the source`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` `is within the period of insurance under` `the policy` `for a liability arising from item` `the source` MEANS
    `falls within the period` `the day`
        (`the day cover under the policy began` `the policy`)
        (`the last days of cover on the works` `the policy`)
        (append (`the events that end cover on the works` `the policy`) `the item's own end events`)
    WHERE
        `the item's own end events` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the source`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST n  THEN
                CONSIDER `the item numbered` n `in` (`the policy`'s `the schedule`)
                WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                WHEN JUST i  THEN append (`the events that end cover on the item as a part` i)
                                         (`the events that end cover on a second-hand item` i)
